          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Dendroidal sets are a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+definition+of+higher+categories"} geometric
            model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} higher
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            (precisely: multi-coloured
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operads"} symmetric operads
            \/
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategories"} symmetric multicategories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            and to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} (∞,1)-operads
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            are to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            A dendroidal set is something that consists of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} trees
            or “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendrices"}> dendrices
            ” in the way that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            consists of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            over them, and so a dendroidal set is a structure defined as having consistent probes by free
            = succeed "-operads." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            More precisely, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
            of dendroidal sets serves to complete the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Cat
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi Operad
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi N
                                  %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi sSet
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi dSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Cat &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; Operad
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{N}}\downarrow &amp;&amp;
                  {}^{\mathllap{N_d}}\downarrow
                  \\\
                  sSet
                  \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                  dSet
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the left vertical functor is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N :
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
            completes this diagram even as a diagram of most of the evident pairs of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            %em
              %a{:href => "#FullDiagram"} The full diagram of relations
            below.
          %p
            Finally, there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            which is the operadic analog of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#DendroidalSets Dendroidal sets
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Operad"} Operad
              for the category of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"}> Set
                  \-enriched;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"}> symmetric
                  ;
              %li
                %p multi-coloured
            %p
              operads, also known as
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategories"} symmetric multicategories
          #FreeOperadCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The symmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Operad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega \hookrightarrow Operad
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Operad"} Operad
              on those
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operads"} symmetric operads
              that are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              on finite rooted non-planar
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trees"} trees
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Trees"}> below
            ) for details on the trees appearing here.
          #DendroidalSet.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong dendroidal set
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of dendroidal sets is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dSet = [\Omega^{op}, Set]
                    \\,.
          %p
            Some
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong terminology and notation
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in \Omega
                a tree, write
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega[T] := \Omega(-,T)
                for the dendroidal set that it
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represents
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a dendroidal set and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                a tree, the set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet(\Omega[T],X) \simeq X(T)
                (using the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
                = succeed "-shaped" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendrices"} dendrices
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                = succeed "-shaped" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong dendrex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
                in a
