          %h3#Trees Trees and their free operads
          %p
            We expand on the notion of symmetric/non-planar trees used in definition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DendroidalSet"}
            of dendroidal sets (see for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Weiss"}> Weiss, section 2.1
            )).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong finite symmetric rooted tree
              – or just
              %strong tree
              for short, in the following – is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T, \leq)
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom"} bottom
                  element;
              %li
                %p
                  for each element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in T
                  the set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi y
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{y \in T | y \leq e\}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
                  under
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            %p
              and equipped with a subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi max
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \subset max(T)
              of the maximal elements of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p One has the following terminology
          .num_defn
            %h6#terminology Terminology
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((T, \leq), L)
              be a tree.
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  An element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in T
                  is called an
                  %strong edge
                  of the tree.
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom"} bottom
                  element is called the
                  %strong root
                  of the tree.
              %li
                %p
                  An edge in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \subset T
                  is a
                  %strong leaf
                  of the tree.
              %li
                %p
                  An edge which is either a leaf or the root is called an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %strong outer edge
              %li
                %p
                  An edge which is neither a leaf nor the root is called an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %strong inner edge
              %li
                %p
                  Given a non-leaf edge
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi e
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e'
                  is called an
                  %strong incoming edge
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  if it is a direct succesor of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi e
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi e
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi e
                            %mo ′
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \leq e'
                      ;
                  %li
                    %p
                      for any
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi T
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in T
                      with
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi e
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi x
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi e
                            %mo ′
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \leq x \leq e'
                      either
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo =
                            %mi e
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = e
                      or
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo =
                              %mi e
                              %mo ′
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = e'
                %p
                  Write
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi in
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in(e)
                  for the set of incoming edges of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi e
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  a non-leaf edge, the subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi e
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi in
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_e := \{e\} \cup in(e)
                  is called a
                  %strong vertex
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo ,
                          %mo ≤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T, \leq)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  is called the
                  %strong outgoing edge
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                  are also called
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      ingoing edges of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mi e
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_e
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi in
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mo =
                          %mi in
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in(v_e) := in(e)
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %strong valence
                  of a vertex
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi in
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert in(v)\vert}
          #ATypicalTree.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p A typical tree as above is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi e
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi f
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mi v
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi b
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi c
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mi u
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mi d
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mi w
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi r
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    {}_{\mathllap{e}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet_v
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; {}_{\mathllap{b}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{c}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; &amp;&amp; \bullet_u &amp; \stackrel{d}{\leftarrow} &amp; \bullet_w
                    \\\
                    \&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{r}}
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p the arrows depict the edges;
              %li
                %p the bullets depict vertices;
              %li
                %p the arrows not starting at a bullet depict leaf edges.
              %li
                %p the arrow not ending at a bullet depicts the root edge.
            %p
              The set of incoming edges of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e,f\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{b,c,d\}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %p
              The valence of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              is 2, that of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              is 3 and that of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              is 0.
            %p
              Notice that there is
              %em no
              order on the incoming edges of any vertex implied, the fact that there is one in the above picture is an artefact of being a planar diagram for visualization purposes. As a tree, the above is
              %em equal
              to, for instance
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi f
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi e
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mi v
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi b
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi c
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mi u
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mi d
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mi w
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi r
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    {}_{\mathllap{f}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{e}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet_v
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; {}_{\mathllap{b}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{c}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; &amp;&amp; \bullet_u &amp; \stackrel{d}{\leftarrow} &amp; \bullet_w
                    \\\
                    \&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{r}}
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\,,
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((T, \leq ), L)
              a tree, the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric operad
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              is the one
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  whose set of colours is is
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  (the set of edges);
              %li
                %p
                  whose operations are freely generated from the set of vertices of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                  goes from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi in
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in(v)
                  to the outgoing edge
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            %p
              More precisely, for every vertex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              and every choice of order
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c_1, \cdots, c_n)
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi in
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in(v)
              there is a generating operation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (c_1, \cdots, c_n) \to c
            %p
              and the action of an element of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in S_n
              takes this to the generator
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (c_{\sigma(1)}, \cdots, c_{\sigma(n)}) \to c
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The operad corresponding to the tree from example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ATypicalTree"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p has six colours;
              %li
                %p has precisely six non-identity operations:
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      the generators
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi v
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi u
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi w
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
                  %li
                    %p
                      the composites
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi u
                            %mo ∘
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \circ (v, id_c, id_d)
                      and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi u
                            %mo ∘
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \circ (id_b, id_c, w)
                      and
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi u
                              %mo ∘
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi v
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi id
                                %mi c
                              %mo ,
                              %mi w
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \circ (v, id_c, w)
          %p
            The inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \hookrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Operad"} Operad
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            on those operads that arise from trees in this way.
          %p Some non-typical trees of importance are the following.
          #LinearTree.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              there is the
              %strong linear tree
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mn 01
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mn 02
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ⋮
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mi n
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L_n
                    \:=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\downarrow^{0}
                    \\\
                    \\bullet_{01}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{1}
                    \\\
                    \\bullet_{02}
                    \\\
                    \\vdots
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{n}
                    }
                    \\right\}
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              colors and only unary operations.
            %p
              The map that sends the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_n
              extends to a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta \hookrightarrow \Omega
            %p
              which exhibits the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
          #Corolla.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              For each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              there is the
              %strong corolla tree
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi l
                                      %mn 1
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                              %mi ⋯
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi l
                                      %mi n
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C_n \coloneqq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    {}_{\mathrlap{l_1}}\searrow &amp; \cdots &amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{l_n}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \downarrow
                    }
                    \\right\}
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              leaves and precisely one vertex.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The trees
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_0
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
              differ.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_0
              is the tree
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\downarrow
                    \\right\}
            %p
              with no vertex, while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
              is the tree
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    }
                    \\right\}
            %p with a single vertex, which has valence 0.
          %h3#OperationsFacesHorns Operations – Faces and horns of trees
          %p
            A dendroidal set encodes composition of
            %em operations
            in analogy to how a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            encodes composition of edges: by way of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
                extensions
            %em faces
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
          %p
            To motivate the definition of dendroidal face maps, first consider the reformulation of simplicial faces under the map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_! : sSet \to dSet
          %p
            Under this embedding the
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
            becomes the operad corresponding to the linear tree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_n
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LinearTree"}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo •
                    %mn 01
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mo •
                    %mn 02
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\stackrel{a}{\to} \bullet_{01} \stackrel{b}{\to} \bullet_{02} \stackrel{c}{\to} \cdots \to \bullet_{(n-1) n} \to
          %p
            with unary operations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo •
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet_{i (i+1)}
          %p
            The face inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i : \Delta[n-1] \to \Delta[n]
            which simplicially omits the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet_{(i-1)i}
            to the unary operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\bullet_{i (i+1)} \circ \bullet_{(i-1) i }
          %p and sends all other generating unary operation to generating unary operations.
          %p From this it is clear that for any tree the map that exhibits the contraction of one edge should be a dendroidal face map. However, there are also some more cases to be taken care of. One has
          %ol
            %li
              %p inner face maps – obtained by contracting an inner edge
            %li
              %p outer face maps – obtained by
              %ol
                %li
                  %p removing an outer input vertex
                %li
                  %p removing a vertex whose output is the root and which has precisely one inner incoming edge (which becomes the new root)
                %li
                  %p a corolla face – any one of the inclusions of the tree with no vertex into a tree with precisely one vertex
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in \Omega
              a tree and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              an
              %em inner edge
              , write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/e
              for the tree obtained by contracting/discarding this inner edge. There is a canonical inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi e
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial_e : T/e \to T
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %p
              This is called an
              %strong inner face map
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          #ExampleForInnerFace.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↙
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi v
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mi e
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T =
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp; v
                    \\\
                    \\searrow &amp; &amp; \searrow^e
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet &amp;\to&amp; \bullet &amp;\to&amp;
                    \\\
                    \\nearrow
                    }
                    \\right\}
            %p then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↙
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T/e =
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\searrow &amp;&amp; \searrow&amp; &amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet &amp;\to&amp; \bullet &amp;\to&amp;
                    \\\
                    \\nearrow
                    }
                    \\right\}
            %p
              and the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi e
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/e \to T
              is the operad morphism that is the identity on the operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\searrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet &amp; \to
                    \\\
                    \\nearrow
                    }
              and which sends the trinary operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \\to &amp; \bullet &amp; \to
                    }
              to the composite trinary operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mi e
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet
                    \\\
                    \&amp; &amp; \searrow^e
                    \\\
                    \&amp; &amp;\to&amp; \bullet &amp;\to&amp;
                    \\\
                    }
          %p
            In contrast to that,
            %em outer
            edges are always removed together:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              is a vertex of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              such that all but one edge incident on it are outer, then denote by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/v
              the tree obtained by discarding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              and all the outer edges indicent on it. There is then again a canonical inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi v
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi v
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial_v : T/v \to T
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is called an
              = succeed "." do
                %strong outer face map
          .num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              With
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              as from example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExampleForInnerFace"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mi e
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mo •
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T/v
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\searrow &amp; &amp; \searrow^e
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet &amp;\to&amp; \bullet &amp;\to&amp;
                    \\\
                    \\nearrow
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              be a corolla tree, example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Corolla"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
              injections of the tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_0
              with no vertex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |
              into the corolla with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              inputs.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ↪
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    | \hookrightarrow
                    \\array{
                    \\searrow &amp;\cdots &amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \bullet
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \downarrow
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              These are called
              %strong corolla face maps
              and counted as
              = succeed "." do
                %em outer face maps
          %p
            In terms of these face maps there is now a notion of
            %em boundary
            and
            %em horn
            of a tree in direct analogy to the notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+simplex"} boundary of a simplex
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            in a simplex.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              be a tree and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Faces
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Faces(T) \subset \Omega_{/T}
              be the set of all its face maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_\alpha \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T]
              , as defined above. The
              %strong boundary
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is the dendroidal set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Faces
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial \Omega[T] := \coprod_{\alpha \in Faces(T)} \partial_\alpha \Omega[T]
            %p
              given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              of all these faces in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega[T]
            %p
              For given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Faces
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in Faces(T)
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %strong horn
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^\alpha[T] \in dSet
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is the union of all faces except this one:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo ≠
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Faces
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi β
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Lambda^\alpha[T]
                    \:=
                    \\coprod_{(\beta \neq \alpha) \in Faces(T)} \partial_\beta \Omega[T]
                    \\,.
            %p
              A horn is called an
              %strong outer horn
              or an
              %strong inner horn
              depending on whether the omitted face is outer or inner, respectively.
            %p
              The inner horn corresponding to the inner face map given by contraction an edge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              is canonically denoted
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi a
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^a \Omega[T]
          %p
            These definitions are due to (
            %a{:href => "#WeissThesis"}> Weiss (thesis)
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#MoerdijkWeiss"}> MoerdijkWeiss
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              This is a genuine generalization of the notion of horns and boundaries of simplices. The outer/inner horns of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
              are taken by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_! : sSet \to dSet
              precisely to the outer/inner hors of the linear tree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_n = i_!(\Delta^n)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_11 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi α
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^\alpha \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T]
              a horn inclusion and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in dSet
              a dendroidal set, an
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
                \-horn in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a morphism of simplicial set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi α
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Lambda^\alpha \Omega[T] \to X
                    \\,.
            %p
              A
              %strong filler
              of this horn in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is an extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi α
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Lambda^\alpha \Omega[T] &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow
                    \\\
                    \\Omega[T]
                    }
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Choices of dendroidal
              %em inner horn
              fillers correspond to
              %em choices of composites
              of operations.
            %p
              A dendrex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega[T] \to X
              encodes a collection of operations and choices of theor composite in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              An inner horn
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi e
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^e \Omega[T] \to X
              encodes a choice of operations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and their composites
              %em except
              a choice for the composition of operations along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            %p
              The outer horn fillers have different interpretation. They correspond to choices of a) inverses of linear operations 2) invertible elements of
              = succeed "-ary" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p
              For more on this see
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
          %h3#SkeletalFiltration Skeletal filtration
          #SkeletalFiltration.num_defn
            %h6#definition_12 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in dSet
              a dendroidal set and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sk
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sk_n(X) \in dSet
              for the dendroidal set which is generated from the non-degenerate
              = succeed "-dendrices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert T\vert} \leq n
            %p The sequence of inclusions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sk
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Sk
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Sk
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sk_0(X) \hookrightarrow Sk_1(X) \hookrightarrow Sk_2(X) \hookrightarrow
                    \\cdots \hookrightarrow X
            %p
              is called the
              %strong skeletal filtration
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#NormalMonomorphisms Normal monomorphisms and normal dendroidal sets
          %p
            A key fact in the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            there are generated under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+simplex"} boundary inclusions
            (indeed the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
            with generating cofibrations the boundary inclusions).
          %p
            For dendroidal sets the boundary inclusions turn out not to generate all monomorphisms, but just a subclass called the
            %em normal
            monomorphisms. We discuss now the definition and some basic propoerties of normal monomorphisms. Most of these are a specialization of the general notion of
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+category#NormalMorphisms"} normal morphisms over a generalized Reedy category
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+category"} generalized Reedy category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_face_maps_are_the_monomorphisms Lemma (face maps are the monomorphisms)
            %p
              The inner and outer face morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_e
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_v
              are precisely the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Lemma 3.1 in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://cat.inist.fr/?aModele=afficheN&cpsidt=20087314"} MoeWei07
          %p
            The
            %strong boundary of a tree
            is the union of all its face dendroidal sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Edges
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi e
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Vertices
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi v
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial \Omega[T] = \cup_{e \in Edges(T)} \Omega[\partial_e T] \cup_{v \in Vertices(T)} \Omega[\partial_v T]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Compare to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+simplex"} boundary of a simplex
          %p
            Analogously then to the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            an edge of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            the union
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi e
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Edges
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi e
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Vertices
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi v
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Lambda^e \Omega[T] = \cup_{e \neq d \in Edges(T)} \Omega[\partial_e T] \cup_{v \in Vertices(T)} \Omega[\partial_v T]
          %p
            of dendroidal sets is the
            %strong inner horn
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            an outer face the union
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi w
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Edges
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi e
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Vertices
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi v
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Lambda^w \Omega[T] = \cup_{e \neq d \in Edges(T)} \Omega[\partial_e T] \cup_{v \neq w \in Vertices(T)} \Omega[\partial_v T]
          %p
            is the
            %strong outer horn
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
          %p
            We have the canonical
            %strong boundary inclusions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T]
          %p
            and
            %strong horn inclusions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi α
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Lambda^\alpha \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T]
                  \\,.
          #NormalMorphism.num_defn
            %h6#definition_13 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              of dendroidal sets is called
              %strong normal
              if for any tree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y(T)
              which does not belong to the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(T)
              has a trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi y
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(T)_y \subset Aut(T)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %p
              A dendroidal set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is called
              %strong normal
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \hookrightarrow X
              is a normal monomorphism.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              This is unrelated to the notion of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+monomorphism"} normal monomorphism
              in a context with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphisms"} zero morphisms
          %p Here are some equivalent characterizations of normality.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A dendroidal set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is normal precisely if for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi Ω
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi nd
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Sk
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi Ω
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi nd
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Sk
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\coprod_{[\Omega[T] \stackrel{nd}{\to} X]} \partial \Omega[T]
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    Sk_n(X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\coprod_{[\Omega[T] \stackrel{nd}{\to} X]} \Omega[T]
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    Sk_{n+1}(X)
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              diagram, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi Sk
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Sk_n(X)\}
              is the skeletal filtration, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SkeletalFiltration"}
              and where the coproduct is over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of non-degenerate dendrices.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
              is normal precisely if for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in \Omega
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(T)
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y(T)-X(T)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
            %p
              Accordingly, a dendroidal set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is normal precisely if for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in \Omega
              the action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(T)
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y(T)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisMoer09"}> CisMoer09, prop 1.5
            ).
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              any morphism between dendroidal sets, then
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  is normal, then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is normal;
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  is normal and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monic
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is normal.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  For every tree
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega[T]
                  is normal.
              %li
                %p
                  For every
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo !
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!(X)
                  is normal.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The class of normal morphisms in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
              is generated from the boundary inclusions under
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"}> pushouts
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+compositions"}> transfinite compositions
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"}> retracts
                  \.
            %p In particular it is closed under these operations.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisMoer09"}> CisMoer09, prop 1.4
            ).
          %h3#BoardmanVogtTensorProduct Boardman-Vogt tensor product
          %p
            As any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            is not the natural one with respect to the inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            into dendroidal sets. The natural monoidal structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Operad"} Operad
            is rather a generalization of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
          #BVTensorProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition_14 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Operad
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Operad
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Operad
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi d
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_d(-\otimes -)
                    \:
                    \\Omega \times \Omega
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Operad \times Operad
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Operad
                    \\stackrel{N_d}{\to}
                    dSet
            %p
              for the functor that forms the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
              of the free operads given by two trees, and then regards the result as a dendroidal set by the dendroidal nerve, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DendroidalNerve"}
            %p
              The
              %strong tensor product of dendroidal sets
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo :
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo ×
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \-\otimes - : dSet \times dSet \to dSet
            %p
              of this functor, hence the unique such functor which preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              in both variables and coincides with the BV-tensor product of operads on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
          %p
            With respect to this tensor product is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
            a colax symmetric monoidal category (
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HeutsHinichMoerdijk13"} Theorem 6.3.4 of HHM13
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ClosedMonoidalStructure"} below
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
              two normal monomorphisms, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalMorphism"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A \otimes Y) \coprod_{A \otimes X} (B \otimes X)
                    \\to
                    B \otimes Y
            %p is also normal.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisMoer09"}> CisMoer09, prop 1.9
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToSimplicialSets Relation to simplicial sets
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            for the tree consisting of a single edge. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega/0
            be the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega/0 \simeq \Delta
            %p
              of the slice with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %p
              Moreover, the over-category of all dendroidal sets over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta := \Omega[0]
              is the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi sSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dSet/\Omega[0] \simeq sSet
                    \\,.
          %p
            By general properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            we have the following
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              The corresponding canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i : \Delta \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \Omega/0 \to \Omega
            %p is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : \Delta \to \Omega
              induces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ↪
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                    %mi dSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (i_! \dashv i^* \dashv i_*)
                    \:
                    sSet
                    \\stackrel{
                    \\overset{i_!}{\hookrightarrow}
                    }{
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{i_*}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    }
                    dSet
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*
                  is given by precomposition with
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
                  defined equivalently as
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                      to
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi i
                                %mo *
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*
                  %li
                    %p
                      the left
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
                      of
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  %li
                    %p
                      the canonical functor
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi sSet
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mo ≃
                              %mi dSet
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo →
                              %mi dSet
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} dSet/\Omega[0] \to dSet
                  %li
                    %p
                      the functor that sends
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi sSet
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in sSet
                      to
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo :
                            %mi T
                            %mo ↦
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %msub
                                        %mi X
                                        %mi n
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi if
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi T
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi is
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi linear
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi with
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi n
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi vertices
                                      %mo ;
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi ∅
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi otherwise
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            i_!(X)
                            \:
                            T
                            \\mapsto
                            \\left\{
                            \\array{
                            X_n &amp; if\,T\,is\,linear\,with\,n\,vertices;
                            \\\
                            \\emptyset &amp; otherwise
                            }
                            \\right.
                            \\,.
            %p
              Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_*
            %p
              Accordingly,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : sSet \hookrightarrow dSet
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+geometric+morphism"} open
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+toposes"} presheaf toposes
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              The dendroidal set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!([n])
              that corresponds to the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              is the linear tree; example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LinearTree"}
              = succeed "-edges:" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                      %mo •
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mn 1
                      %mo •
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mn 2
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo •
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi n
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i([n])
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    \\stackrel{0}{\to}
                    \\bullet
                    \\stackrel{1}{\to}
                    \\bullet
                    \\stackrel{2}{\to}
                    \\cdots
                    \\bullet
                    \\stackrel{n}{\to}
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              We think of each bullet as a unary operation – an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              –
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi n
                    %mo •
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{n}{\to}\bullet \stackrel{n+1}{\to}
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              to the object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            %p
              Notice that this is hence Poincaré-dual to how one tends to visualize
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
              itself
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [n] = (0 \to 1 \to 2 \to \cdots \to n)
            %p
              and how one tends to visualize morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \to (n+1)
          %p
            The embedding of simplicial sets into dendroidal sets compatibly relates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} Cartesian monoidal structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (sSet, \times)
            with the
            %a{:href => "#BoardmanVogtTensorProduct"} Boardman-Vogt monoidal structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi dSet
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi BV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dSet, \otimes_{BV})
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p The functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_! : (sSet, \times) \to (dSet, \otimes_{BV})
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in sSet
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_!(X \times Y) \simeq i_!(Y) \otimes_{BV} i_!(Y)
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
            %p
              Moreover,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i_! \dashv i^*)
              respects the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              of dendroidal sets, prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheClosedMonoidalStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in sSet
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in dSet
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi D
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi BV
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^* [i_!(X), D]_{BV} \simeq [X, i^*(D)]
                ;
            %p and hence in particular
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi BV
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^* [i_!(X), i_!(Y)]_{BV} \simeq [X, Y]
                \.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#MoerdijkWeiss"}> Moerdijk-Weiss, prop. 5.3
            ).
          %h3#RelationToOperads
            Relation to
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            By the general notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Operad
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \hookrightarrow Operad
            from def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeOperadCategory"}
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            operation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            with values in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          #DendroidalNerve.num_defn
            %h6#definition_15 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Operad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O \in Operad
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+nerve"} dendroidal nerve
              is the dendroidal set given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Operad
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_d(O) : T \mapsto Hom_{Operad}(T, O)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This extends to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %mi Operad
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_d : Operad \to dSet
                    \\,.
          %p
            By general properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
            we have:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p The dendroidal nerve has the following properties.
            %ul
              %li
                %p It extends the simplicial nerve of operads in that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mi N
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        i^* \circ N_d = N
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  It has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi d
                        %mo :
                        %mi dSet
                        %mo →
                        %mi Operad
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\tau_d : dSet \to Operad
                %p
                  given by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi d
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi d
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi id
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\tau_d \circ N_d \simeq id
                        \\,.
          %p
            See for instance (
            %a{:href => "#MoerdijkWeiss"}> Moerdijk-Weiss, section 4
            ).
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a dendroidal set,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_d(X)
            is also called the
            %strong operad generated by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            In conclusion we find
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi d
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Operad
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi d
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi d
                  %mi dSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\tau_d \dashv N_d)
                  \:
                  Operad
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\tau_d}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{N_d}{\hookrightarrow}}
                  dSet
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is compatible with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
            as defined
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#BoardmanVogtTensorProduct"} above
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Operad
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_d : (dSet, \otimes) \to (Operad, \otimes_{BV})
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in dSet
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau_d(X \otimes Y ) \simeq \tau_d(X) \otimes_{BV} \tau_d(Y)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#MoerdijkWeiss"}> Moerdijk-Weiss, prop. 5.2
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_d N_d \simeq id
              in particular we have for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Operad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P, Q \in Operad
              an isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi P
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                    %mi Q
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau_d (N_d(P) \otimes N_d(Q)) \simeq P \otimes_{BV} Q
                    \\,.
          %h3#HomotopyCoherentNerve
            Relation to
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          %p
            The dendroidal nerve of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
            discussed
            %a{:href => "#RelationToOperads"} above
            is important for setting up the model of dendroidal sets. But the usefulness of the model comes from its relation to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+operads"} topological operads
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            that sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+categories"} sSet-enriched categories
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Operad
                    %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Operad_sSet
            for the category of
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+operads"} simplicial operads
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi H
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Operad
                    %mi sSet
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Operad
                    %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  W_H : Operad_sSet \to Operad_sSet
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+resolution"} Boardman-Vogt resolution
            functor.
          %p The restriction of this along the inclusion of free Set-operads
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Operad
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Operad
                    %mi sSet
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi H
                  %msub
                    %mi Operad
                    %mi sSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega \hookrightarrow Operad
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  Operad_{sSet}
                  \\stackrel{W_H}{\to}
                  Operad_{sSet}
                  \\,,
          %p
            which will also be denoted just
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_H
            in the following, canonically induces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
            functors:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_16 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+homotopy+coherent+nerve"} dendroidal homotopy coherent nerve
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+operad"} simplicial operad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is the dendroidal set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi hcN
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hcN_d(P)
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi hcN
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Operad
                          %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    hcN_d(P) : T \mapsto Hom_{Operad_{sSet}}(W_H(T), P)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This extends to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi hcN
                      %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Operad
                      %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    hcN_d : Operad_{sSet} \to dSet
                    \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_17 Definition
            %p We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi H
                    %mo :
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Operad
                      %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert -\vert}_H : dSet \to Operad_{sSet}
            %p
              (or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_!
              as
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} here
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} realization
          %p
            Via this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi H
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi hcN
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Operad
                    %mi sSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi dSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ({\vert -\vert}_H \dashv hcN_d)
                  \:
                  Operad_{sSet}
                  \\to dSet
          %p we may understand generally the theory of dendroidal sets as being about BV-resolutions of simplicial operads.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Operad
                        %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \in Operad_{sSet}
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              of simplicial operads
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi hcN
                          %mi d
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_H(P) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    {\vert hcN_d P \vert}_H
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+resolution"} Boardman-Vogt resolution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_H(P)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              and the homotopy-realization of its homotopy-coherent dendroidal nerve.
          %p
            All of this is an operadic generalization of the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+quasi-categories+and+simplicial+categories"} relation between quasi-categories and simplicial categories
          %h3#FullDiagram The full diagram of relations
          %p
            The above functors between dendroidal sets and simplicial sets (
            %a{:href => "#RelationToSimplicialSets"}> here
            ) and operads (
            %a{:href => "#RelationToOperads"}> here
            ) arrange into the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi sSet
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %munder
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo *
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo !
                        %mtd
                          %mi dSet
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi τ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi N
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi τ
                                  %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi N
                                %mi d
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Cat
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %munder
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo *
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo !
                        %mtd
                          %mi Operad
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  sSet
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\overset{i_!}{\to}}{\underset{i^*}{\leftarrow}}&amp;
                  dSet
                  \\\
                  {}^\mathllap{\tau} \downarrow
                  \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{N}}
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  {}^{\mathllap{\tau_d}}
                  \\downarrow
                  \\uparrow^{N_d}
                  \\\
                  Cat
                  \&amp;
                  \\stackrel{\overset{j_!}{\to}}{\underset{j^*}{\leftarrow}}
                  \&amp;
                  Operad
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            where functors on the left and on top are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoints
            to those on the right and on the bottom, respectively.
          %p
            This commutes in three of four possible ways, up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            in that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mo !
                      %mi τ
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_! \tau \simeq \tau_d i_!
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N j^* \simeq i^* N_d
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mi N
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_! N \simeq N_d j_!
                \.
          %p
            There is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi d
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau i^* \Rightarrow j^* \tau_d
                  \\,,
          %p but not all of its components are isomorphisms.
          %p
            Moreover,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N, N_d
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo !
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!, j_!
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functors"} full and faithful functors
            and hence (see the properties of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                      %mi N
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau N \simeq id
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi d
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_d N_d \simeq id
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^* i_! \simeq id
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mo !
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^* j_! \simeq id
                \.
          %h2#structure_on_
            Structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
          %p
            Some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
            carried by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
          %h3#ClosedMonoidalStructure Homotopical monoidal structure
          %p
            %a{:href => "#HeutsHinichMoerdijk13"} Heuts-Hinich-Moerdijk 13, section 6.3
          %h3#enriched_structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            \-enriched structure
          %p
            Using the fact that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            dendroidal sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,D]
            for dendroidal sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi dSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi SSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^* : dSet \to SSet
            we obtain canonically the structure of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
            \/
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
            with the hom-simplicial set between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            being
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*[C,D]
          %h3#model_category_structure Model category structure
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
            carries the Cisinski-Moerdijk
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
          %p
            Together with the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi dSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*: dSet \to sSet
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
            (with respect to the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
            is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
            (but not, without further work, an
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibration+of+dendroidal+sets"} Cartesian fibration of dendroidal sets
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+dendroidal+fibration"} minimal dendroidal fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"}> simplicial set
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globular+set"} globular set
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+set"} cubical set
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+set"} cellular set
          %h2#References References
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+Heuts"}> Gijs Heuts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em Simplicial and Dendroidal Homotopy Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 75
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-10447-3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-031-10447-3
          %p Surveys:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                %em Lectures on dendroidal sets
                , lectures given at the Barcelona workshop on
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.crm.es/HigherCategories/"} Simplicial methods in higher categories
                (2008) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.crm.cat/HigherCategories/hc1.pdf"}> preliminary writeup
                )
            %li#Weiss
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ittay+Weiss"}> Ittay Weiss
                ,
                %em From operads to dendroidal sets
                , in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
          %p Dendroidal sets were introduced in
          %ul
            %li#MoerdijkWeiss
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ittay+Weiss"} Ittay Weiss
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dendroidal sets
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://msp.warwick.ac.uk/agt/2007/07/p056.xhtml"} doi:10.2140/agt.2007.7.1441
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0701293"} arXiv:math.AT/0701293
          %p
            A discussion of dendroidal inner Kan complexes (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ittay+Weiss"} Ittay Weiss
              = succeed "," do
                %em On inner Kan complexes in the category of dendroidal sets
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0701295"} math.CT/0701295
          %p The thesis
          %ul#WeissThesis
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ittay+Weiss"}> Ittay Weiss
              ,
              %em Dendroidal sets
              PhD thesis (
              %a{:href => "http://igitur-archive.library.uu.nl/dissertations/2007-0918-200833/UUindex.html"}> web
              )
          %p contains essentially the material of these two articles, together with a discussion of broad posets.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+Segal+operads"} model structure for Segal operads
            was constructed in
          %ul
            %li#CisinskiMoerdijk13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dendroidal Segal spaces and infinity-operads
              %strong 6
              3 (2013) 675-794 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1010.4956"}> arXiv:1010.4956
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/jtopol/jtt004"} doi:10.1112/jtopol/jtt004
          %p Normal morphisms of dendroidal sets are discussed for instance around prop. 1.4 of
          %ul
            %li#CisMoer09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em Dendroidal sets as models for homotopy operads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0902.1954"}> arXiv:0902.1954
              )
